Total Amiga Assembler
---------------------
System Requirements: Commodore Amiga with at least 512K 
of RAM. Whilst some programs will run on all versions of
the Amiga's operating system those which use GadTools,
the ASL file requester etc., require Release 2 or greater.
To edit/assemble the examples the user should have a 
suitable text editor, assembler and linker available. 
These items are available from both commercial and 
public domain sources.

The Official Amiga Include Files
--------------------------------
One thing that A68k users do need to be aware of is 
the fact that they will NOT get the official Amiga
include files with their assembler. It is possible however 
that some high-level language users will already have 
suitable include files, SAS C for instance provides
these as part of the compiler package, but if not two options 
are available: Firstly, the files can be purchased from Amiga
Technologies. Secondly, the appropriate definitions etc.,
can be typed in from sources such the Addison Wesley RKM
Includes & Autodocs reference manual. 

I've used this latter approach for a number of programs in this
book in order to allow the examples to be assembled without the
official includes. You'll find details in the text file called
ImportantNotes!


